ason for  that is because the new iPhone 12 is  gonna have a smaller 5.4 inch display  which makes it cheaper to produce and  they'll actually offer a plus sized  iPhone 12 model which  be identical in specs but have a 6.1  inch display for 750 dollars which is  ironically the same exact size and price  as the iPhones had are at launch this is  a genius move because those who don't  want a small 5.4 inch display have the  option of paying $100 more for the max  model instead of having to go from one  of the more expensive pro models and  speaking of those the iPhone 12 pro is  rumored to also get a 6.1 inch display  and the pro max model will get a 6 point  7 inch display this actually makes the  most sense because Apple will only have  three display sizes for a total of four  iPhone models making it cheaper to  manufacture compared to having four  different sizes now for that base five  point four inch model it could actually  share the same exact body as the iPhone  se except without the home button and  with a notch bringing that 4.7 inch  display size up to five point four  inches so there are even less  manufacturing costs for Apple leading to  the new low price of only six hundred  and fifty dollars now I don't know if  you guys remember all of those leaks  about the iPhone se coming with face ID  a notch and an OLED display well it  seems like those leaks were actually the  5.4 inch iPhone 12 so this points to  every iPhone in the 20/20 lineup finally  getting in oled display and just like  before we can expect every single iphone  this year to come with the new 5  nanometer a 14 Bionic chip which will be  incredibly powerful we can also expect  the entire lineup to start with 128  gigabytes of base storage and this would  make sense because it's easier and  cheaper to mass-produce that based  storage size for the entire lineup just  like they've already done for the iPad  pro lots of rumors are also pointing to  the iPhone 12 no longer coming with ear  pods 