tz display on  the iPhone 12 Pro this year they're in  trouble because basically every other  Android phone already has a high refresh  rate display and the reason for LTP o  next year would be to help save battery  life and maybe even add an always-on  display feature rumors are also pointing  to a new display with 10-bit color depth  but I don't expect it to get much  brighter  the iPhone 11 pro is already incredibly  bright the iPhone 12 pro max model is  rumored to get a larger 6.7 inch display  possibly with slimmer bezels in a  smaller notch but they'll most likely  have to make the phone itself a little  bit larger to fit that display it will  most likely also come with 5g which I  personally don't care about at all since  4G is fast enough on my iPhone 11 pro  but for the new iPhone 12 lineup the  millimeter wave 5g tech will probably  only come on the pro models in the  cheaper iPhone 12 models might simply  get the sub 6 5g which is more like  faster 4G instead of real 5g  there's a chance that the pro models  will also come with the same lidar  scanner that came on the 20/20 iPad pro  now you might be asking what's the point  of that scanner well it seems as though  Apple will have some surprises for us in  terms of this new sensor at their WWDC  event on June 22nd and once again we  should expect to see the same lightning  port as before so no USB C port this  year and finally more rumors are  pointing to the pro models getting  bumped up to 6 gigabytes of RAM  alongside the new 128 gigabyte based  storage at the same prices as last year  $1000 for the pro and $1,100 for the pro  max now in terms of when we should  expect the release date some new rumours  are showing that these iPhones will be  getting delayed pointing to a quarter  for release date but don't freak out  quarter 4 actually starts in October  just three weeks after the usual  September event date so if we do get  delays it'll most likely be like the  iPhone 10 R which came out on October 